            <ArticleTitle>A Pancreatic Fistula as a Rare Complication of Laparascopic Radical Nephrectomy: A Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.eucr.2017.02.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an unusual case of pancreatic fistula after transperitoneal laparoscopic left radical nephrectomy. A 43 years old male patient presented with severe abdominal pain and abdominal distension 71 day after the surgery. Computerized tomography (CT) demonstrated a large fluid collection in the operated renal fossa. The treatment, which comprised percutaneous drainage led to a closure of the fistula 20 days after therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
